{
  "material": "trench_wall",
  "kind": "ground",
  "space": "wall",
  "formula": "wall v1: the strip of lib/strip.py, size_m [u, v] at output_px [w, h], v up the map; base = the loam and soil sets each tiled at its tile_size_m along u and v, blended at soil.share, gained to albedo_target; per wall row the topsoil band (the params' topsoil_m below the row's top, its edge moved by up to TOPSOIL_EDGE_M of value noise on TOPSOIL_LOBE_M cells, feathered over TOPSOIL_FEATHER_M) blended to topsoil at TOPSOIL_LEVEL, ROOTS_PER_M root lines per metre hanging ROOT_LEN_M from the lip within lib.strip.TOPSOIL_ROOTS_M, ROOT_PX wide, in roots, the clod spill (lib.strip.SPILL_M at the row's foot, its top moved by SPILL_EDGE_M of noise, feathered over SPILL_FEATHER_M) blended to spill at SPILL_LEVEL; the floor row gained to floor_albedo; normal = the sets' normals blended at soil.share, plus on the wall rows spade facets: a lattice of facets.size_m cells jittered by FACET_JITTER, each tilted by a seeded tangent of at most 2 relief_m / size_m across u and v, added to the normals' x and y; mask R 0, G the sets' AO, B 0, A 1 - roughness; detail albedo = the detail set's diffuse as grey at its size with a linear mean of 0.5; 8-bit sRGB albedos",
  "pillow": "12.3.0",
  "constants": {
    "MAX_OUTPUT_PX": 2048,
    "TOPSOIL_LEVEL": 0.85,
